-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part wra1 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-04; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Cases for wra1-seat.l4: one or more for every question, with the facts a real person in the seat would state.
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the section named in the comment above it, not from the output.
-- A figure such as 500 or a day such as 1 April 2026 is an invented test figure: the Act supplies none of them.
-- "I do not know" is the person's answer to a fact only regulations decide; the Act then answers NOTHING unless some other fact decides.

§ `Part 1 Chapter 1 -- entitlement`

-- s 1(2)(a): an individual who is not a member of a couple may be awarded it. Arguments: claiming jointly, I am a member of a couple, married or civil partners, same household, living together as if married
#ASSERT `Under section 1(2), may universal credit be awarded to me` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a member of a couple claiming alone: s 2(2) lets regulations allow it, and s 1(2) does not say no, so the Act does not answer
#ASSERT `Under section 1(2), may universal credit be awarded to me` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 1(2)(b) with s 39(1)(a): joint claimants who are married and in the same household are a couple
#ASSERT `Under section 1(2), may universal credit be awarded to me` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 1(2)(b) with s 39(1)(b): not married but living together as if married
#ASSERT `Under section 1(2), may universal credit be awarded to me` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- two people claiming jointly who are not a couple (flatmates): s 1(2) does not say they may not
#ASSERT `Under section 1(2), may universal credit be awarded to me` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 4(1)(a): 18 is old enough; under 18 the 'no' is provisional because regulations may prescribe a different minimum age (s 4(3)); 40 is old enough
#ASSERT `Under section 4(1)(a), am I at least 18 years old` 18 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 4(1)(a), am I at least 18 years old` 17 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 4(1)(a), am I at least 18 years old` 40 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 4(1)(b): the condition is that the person has NOT reached the qualifying age
#ASSERT `Under section 4(1)(b), have I not yet reached the qualifying age for state pension credit` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 4(1)(b), have I not yet reached the qualifying age for state pension credit` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- s 4(1)(c): England, Scotland and Wales are in Great Britain; Northern Ireland and places outside the United Kingdom are not
#ASSERT `Under section 4(1)(c), am I in Great Britain` Wales EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 4(1)(c), am I in Great Britain` Scotland EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 4(1)(c), am I in Great Britain` `Greater London` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 4(1)(c), am I in Great Britain` `England outside Greater London` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 4(1)(c), am I in Great Britain` `Northern Ireland` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 4(1)(c), am I in Great Britain` `outside the United Kingdom` EQUALS FALSE
-- Arguments: age, reached the qualifying age for state pension credit, where I am, receiving education, accepted the up-to-date commitment, accepted it as prescribed
-- all five conditions met: at least 18, below the qualifying age, in Great Britain, not receiving education, commitment accepted
#ASSERT `Under section 4(1), do I meet the basic conditions` 30 FALSE Wales `s 1(1) what I know: no` TRUE `s 1(1) what I know: yes` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- under 18: that limb is provisional (s 4(3)), and the others hold, so the Act does not answer
#ASSERT `Under section 4(1), do I meet the basic conditions` 17 FALSE Wales `s 1(1) what I know: no` TRUE `s 1(1) what I know: yes` EQUALS NOTHING
-- in Northern Ireland: a 'no', but s 4(2) lets regulations make exceptions, so it is provisional
#ASSERT `Under section 4(1), do I meet the basic conditions` 30 FALSE `Northern Ireland` `s 1(1) what I know: no` TRUE `s 1(1) what I know: yes` EQUALS NOTHING
-- at the qualifying age for state pension credit: a provisional 'no'
#ASSERT `Under section 4(1), do I meet the basic conditions` 70 TRUE Scotland `s 1(1) what I know: no` TRUE `s 1(1) what I know: yes` EQUALS NOTHING
-- receiving education: a provisional 'no'
#ASSERT `Under section 4(1), do I meet the basic conditions` 30 FALSE Wales `s 1(1) what I know: yes` TRUE `s 1(1) what I know: yes` EQUALS NOTHING
-- not accepted the commitment: a provisional 'no'
#ASSERT `Under section 4(1), do I meet the basic conditions` 30 FALSE Wales `s 1(1) what I know: no` FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: yes` EQUALS NOTHING
-- do not know whether I am receiving education as the regulations define it, all else holds
#ASSERT `Under section 4(1), do I meet the basic conditions` 30 FALSE Wales `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` TRUE `s 1(1) what I know: yes` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 3(1) needs the basic conditions AND the financial conditions of s 5(1); the prescribed amounts of capital and the prescribed minimum are for regulations, so the Act does not answer even when the basic conditions are met
#ASSERT `Under section 3(1), am I entitled to universal credit` 30 FALSE Wales `s 1(1) what I know: no` TRUE `s 1(1) what I know: yes` EQUALS NOTHING
-- a provisional 'no' on the basic conditions leaves the Act silent as well
#ASSERT `Under section 3(1), am I entitled to universal credit` 30 FALSE `outside the United Kingdom` `s 1(1) what I know: no` TRUE `s 1(1) what I know: yes` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 8(1): the balance of the maximum amount less the deductions: 500 - 100 - 20 = 380
#ASSERT `Under section 8(1), what is the amount of my award for the period` 500 100 20 EQUALS JUST 380
-- no deductions: the whole maximum amount
#ASSERT `Under section 8(1), what is the amount of my award for the period` 500 0 0 EQUALS JUST 500
-- deductions equal to the maximum amount leave nothing: 0
#ASSERT `Under section 8(1), what is the amount of my award for the period` 120 100 20 EQUALS JUST 0

§ `Part 1 Chapter 2 -- claimant responsibilities`

-- s 14(5): 'if, and only if' I accept the most up-to-date version in the manner prescribed. Arguments: accepted the up-to-date version, accepted in the manner prescribed
#ASSERT `Under section 14(5), have I accepted my claimant commitment` TRUE `s 1(1) what I know: yes` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 14(5), have I accepted my claimant commitment` TRUE `s 1(1) what I know: no` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 14(5), have I accepted my claimant commitment` TRUE `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 14(5), have I accepted my claimant commitment` FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 19(6)(a): a single person who is responsible for the child. Arguments: member of a couple, I am responsible, my partner is responsible, jointly nominated me
#ASSERT `Under section 19(6), am I the responsible carer for my child` FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: yes` `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 19(6), am I the responsible carer for my child` FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: no` `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 19(6)(b): a member of a couple where one of the two is responsible AND the couple has jointly nominated me
#ASSERT `Under section 19(6), am I the responsible carer for my child` TRUE `s 1(1) what I know: yes` `s 1(1) what I know: no` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 19(6), am I the responsible carer for my child` TRUE `s 1(1) what I know: no` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 19(6), am I the responsible carer for my child` TRUE `s 1(1) what I know: yes` `s 1(1) what I know: no` `s 1(1) what I know: no` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 19(6), am I the responsible carer for my child` TRUE `s 1(1) what I know: no` `s 1(1) what I know: no` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 19(6), am I the responsible carer for my child` TRUE `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Arguments: limited capability for work and work-related activity, caring responsibilities, carer of a child under 1, carer of a child aged 1, carer of a child aged 2, limited capability for work, regulations place me in 19, in 20, in 21
-- none of the descriptions applies: section 22, all work-related requirements
#ASSERT `Under section 13(3), which group of claimants am I in` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: no` `s 1(1) what I know: no` `s 1(1) what I know: no` EQUALS JUST `all work-related requirements`
-- s 19(2)(a): limited capability for work and work-related activity: no work-related requirements, whatever the regulations say
#ASSERT `Under section 13(3), which group of claimants am I in` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` EQUALS JUST `no work-related requirements`
-- s 19(2)(b), (c)
#ASSERT `Under section 13(3), which group of claimants am I in` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: no` `s 1(1) what I know: no` `s 1(1) what I know: no` EQUALS JUST `no work-related requirements`
#ASSERT `Under section 13(3), which group of claimants am I in` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: no` `s 1(1) what I know: no` `s 1(1) what I know: no` EQUALS JUST `no work-related requirements`
-- s 20(1)(a): the responsible carer for a child aged 1: a work-focused interview requirement only
#ASSERT `Under section 13(3), which group of claimants am I in` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: no` `s 1(1) what I know: no` `s 1(1) what I know: no` EQUALS JUST `work-focused interview requirement only`
-- s 21(1)(aa) and (a): a child aged 2, or limited capability for work: interview and work preparation requirements only
#ASSERT `Under section 13(3), which group of claimants am I in` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: no` `s 1(1) what I know: no` `s 1(1) what I know: no` EQUALS JUST `work-focused interview and work preparation requirements only`
#ASSERT `Under section 13(3), which group of claimants am I in` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `s 1(1) what I know: no` `s 1(1) what I know: no` `s 1(1) what I know: no` EQUALS JUST `work-focused interview and work preparation requirements only`
-- do not know whether regulations describe me under section 19(2)(d), and no other description applies: the Act does not say which group
#ASSERT `Under section 13(3), which group of claimants am I in` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` `s 1(1) what I know: no` `s 1(1) what I know: no` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 19(1): the Secretary of State may not impose any work-related requirement on a claimant falling within section 19; outside it the section is silent
#ASSERT `Under section 19(1), may the Secretary of State impose a work-related requirement on me` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 19(1), may the Secretary of State impose a work-related requirement on me` `s 1(1) what I know: no` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 19(1), may the Secretary of State impose a work-related requirement on me` `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 20(2), (3): only a work-focused interview requirement may be imposed on a claimant within section 20
#ASSERT `Under section 20(2), may the Secretary of State impose this requirement on me` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` `work-focused interview requirement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 20(2), may the Secretary of State impose this requirement on me` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` `work search requirement` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 20(2), may the Secretary of State impose this requirement on me` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` `work preparation requirement` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 20(2), may the Secretary of State impose this requirement on me` `s 1(1) what I know: no` `work-focused interview requirement` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 21(2), (3), (4): a work preparation requirement and a work-focused interview requirement, and no other
#ASSERT `Under section 21(2), may the Secretary of State impose this requirement on me` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` `work preparation requirement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 21(2), may the Secretary of State impose this requirement on me` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` `work-focused interview requirement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 21(2), may the Secretary of State impose this requirement on me` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` `work availability requirement` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 21(2), may the Secretary of State impose this requirement on me` `s 1(1) what I know: no` `work preparation requirement` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 22(2): a work search requirement and a work availability requirement, except in prescribed circumstances. Arguments: within section 22, prescribed circumstances apply, the requirement
#ASSERT `Under section 22(2), must the Secretary of State impose this requirement on me` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` `s 1(1) what I know: no` `work search requirement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 22(2), must the Secretary of State impose this requirement on me` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` `s 1(1) what I know: no` `work availability requirement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 22(2), must the Secretary of State impose this requirement on me` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` `work search requirement` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 22(2), must the Secretary of State impose this requirement on me` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` `work availability requirement` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 22(2), must the Secretary of State impose this requirement on me` `s 1(1) what I know: no` `s 1(1) what I know: no` `work search requirement` EQUALS NOTHING
-- the other two requirements are a power in s 22(3), not a duty
#ASSERT `Under section 22(2), must the Secretary of State impose this requirement on me` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` `s 1(1) what I know: no` `work preparation requirement` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 22(3): either or both of a work-focused interview requirement and a work preparation requirement
#ASSERT `Under section 22(3), may the Secretary of State impose this requirement on me` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` `work-focused interview requirement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 22(3), may the Secretary of State impose this requirement on me` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` `work preparation requirement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 22(3), may the Secretary of State impose this requirement on me` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` `work search requirement` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 22(3), may the Secretary of State impose this requirement on me` `s 1(1) what I know: no` `work preparation requirement` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 24(4): the manner is the Secretary of State's to determine only if the notice is not included in the claimant commitment
#ASSERT `Under section 24(4), is notice of the requirement in the manner the Secretary of State may determine` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 24(4), is notice of the requirement in the manner the Secretary of State may determine` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 24(5): 13 weeks from 1 March 2026 end on 30 May 2026. Arguments: first day of the 13 weeks, the day asked about, prescribed circumstances apply, recently a victim
#ASSERT `Under section 24(5)(b), may the Secretary of State impose another requirement on me on that day` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) `s 1(1) what I know: yes` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 24(5)(b), may the Secretary of State impose another requirement on me on that day` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 30 5 2026) `s 1(1) what I know: yes` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 24(5)(b), may the Secretary of State impose another requirement on me on that day` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 5 2026) `s 1(1) what I know: yes` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 24(5)(b), may the Secretary of State impose another requirement on me on that day` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) `s 1(1) what I know: yes` `s 1(1) what I know: no` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 24(5)(b), may the Secretary of State impose another requirement on me on that day` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Arguments: what I failed to do, within section 22, had a good reason, placement of a prescribed description, misconduct, voluntary, loss of pay disregarded
-- s 26(2)(b): failing for no good reason to apply for a particular vacancy
#ASSERT `Under section 26(2), is my failure sanctionable under section 26` `s 26(2)(b) failing to apply for a particular vacancy` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` FALSE FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- with a good reason it is not a failure
#ASSERT `Under section 26(2), is my failure sanctionable under section 26` `s 26(2)(b) failing to apply for a particular vacancy` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` TRUE `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` FALSE FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 26(2)(c)
#ASSERT `Under section 26(2), is my failure sanctionable under section 26` `s 26(2)(c) not taking up an offer of paid work` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` FALSE FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 26(2)(a): the placement must be of a prescribed description
#ASSERT `Under section 26(2), is my failure sanctionable under section 26` `s 26(2)(a) failing to undertake a work placement` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: yes` FALSE FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not known whether the placement was of a prescribed description
#ASSERT `Under section 26(2), is my failure sanctionable under section 26` `s 26(2)(a) failing to undertake a work placement` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` FALSE FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 26(2)(d): voluntarily and for no good reason
#ASSERT `Under section 26(2), is my failure sanctionable under section 26` `s 26(2)(d) ceasing paid work or losing pay` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` FALSE TRUE `s 1(1) what I know: no` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 26(2)(d): by reason of misconduct, whatever the reason given
#ASSERT `Under section 26(2), is my failure sanctionable under section 26` `s 26(2)(d) ceasing paid work or losing pay` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` TRUE `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` TRUE FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: no` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- voluntarily but with a good reason
#ASSERT `Under section 26(2), is my failure sanctionable under section 26` `s 26(2)(d) ceasing paid work or losing pay` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` TRUE `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` FALSE TRUE `s 1(1) what I know: no` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 26(5)(b): loss of pay below the prescribed level, disregarded by regulations
#ASSERT `Under section 26(2), is my failure sanctionable under section 26` `s 26(2)(d) ceasing paid work or losing pay` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` TRUE FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: yes` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not known whether regulations disregard the loss
#ASSERT `Under section 26(2), is my failure sanctionable under section 26` `s 26(2)(d) ceasing paid work or losing pay` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` TRUE FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 26(2) applies to a claimant falling within section 22
#ASSERT `Under section 26(2), is my failure sanctionable under section 26` `s 26(2)(b) failing to apply for a particular vacancy` `s 1(1) what I know: no` FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` FALSE FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 26(6)(b): not exceeding three years: 1 January 2026 to 31 December 2028 is three years; a day more is not
#ASSERT `Under section 26(6)(b), does the period of my reduction not exceed three years` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 12 2028) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 26(6)(b), does the period of my reduction not exceed three years` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2029) EQUALS FALSE
-- Arguments: failed a work-related requirement, failed a section 23 requirement, had a good reason, also sanctionable under section 26
#ASSERT `Under section 27(2), is my failure sanctionable under section 27` TRUE FALSE FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: no` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 27(2), is my failure sanctionable under section 27` FALSE TRUE FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: no` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 27(2), is my failure sanctionable under section 27` TRUE FALSE TRUE `s 1(1) what I know: no` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 27(2), is my failure sanctionable under section 27` FALSE FALSE FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 27(3): not sanctionable here if also sanctionable under section 26
#ASSERT `Under section 27(2), is my failure sanctionable under section 27` TRUE FALSE FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: yes` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 27(2), is my failure sanctionable under section 27` TRUE FALSE FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 27(5)(b): 26 weeks is 182 days
#ASSERT `Under section 27(5)(b), does the fixed period not exceed 26 weeks` 182 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 27(5)(b), does the fixed period not exceed 26 weeks` 183 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 27(5)(b), does the fixed period not exceed 26 weeks` 181 EQUALS TRUE
-- s 28(1): regulations may provide hardship payments where the award is reduced under section 26 or 27 and the claimant is or will be in hardship. Arguments: regulations provide, award reduced, in hardship
#ASSERT `Under section 28(1), may a hardship payment be made to me` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` TRUE `s 1(1) what I know: yes` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 28(1), may a hardship payment be made to me` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` TRUE `s 1(1) what I know: no` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 28(1), may a hardship payment be made to me` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: yes` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 28(1), may a hardship payment be made to me` `s 1(1) what I know: no` TRUE `s 1(1) what I know: yes` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 28(1), may a hardship payment be made to me` `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` TRUE `s 1(1) what I know: yes` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 29(1): such person as the Secretary of State may authorise
#ASSERT `Under section 29(1), may this person exercise the functions of the Secretary of State under sections 13 to 25` `a local authority` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 29(1), may this person exercise the functions of the Secretary of State under sections 13 to 25` `a local authority` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 29(1), may this person exercise the functions of the Secretary of State under sections 13 to 25` `the Secretary of State` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Part 1 Chapter 3 -- supplementary and general`

-- s 33(1): the benefits listed are abolished; the list is not said to be closed
#ASSERT `Under section 33(1), has my old benefit been abolished` `housing benefit` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 33(1), has my old benefit been abolished` `child tax credit` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 33(1), has my old benefit been abolished` `income support` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 33(1), has my old benefit been abolished` `personal independence payment` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 33(1), has my old benefit been abolished` `universal credit` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 37(1): both limbs are needed
#ASSERT `Under section 37(1), do I have limited capability for work on the Act's own test` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 37(1), do I have limited capability for work on the Act's own test` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 37(1), do I have limited capability for work on the Act's own test` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- s 37(2): both limbs are needed
#ASSERT `Under section 37(2), do I have limited capability for work-related activity on the Act's own test` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 37(2), do I have limited capability for work-related activity on the Act's own test` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 37(2), do I have limited capability for work-related activity on the Act's own test` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- s 39(1)(a): married or civil partners AND the same household; (b): not married but living together as if married. Arguments: married or civil partners, same household, living together as if married
#ASSERT `Under section 39(1), are the other person and I a couple` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 39(1), are the other person and I a couple` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 39(1), are the other person and I a couple` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 39(1), are the other person and I a couple` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 39(1), are the other person and I a couple` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Arguments: married, same household, living together, regulations disregard the marriage, treat us as living together, what they say about our household
-- married but in different households, and regulations treat us as members of the same household (s 39(3)(c))
#ASSERT `Under section 39(3), are the other person and I a couple once the regulations are applied` TRUE FALSE FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: no` `s 1(1) what I know: no` `s 39(3) the regulations treat us as members of the same household` EQUALS TRUE
-- not married, not in the same household, and regulations treat us as living together as if married (s 39(3)(b))
#ASSERT `Under section 39(3), are the other person and I a couple once the regulations are applied` FALSE FALSE FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: no` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` `s 39(3) the regulations say nothing about it in our case` EQUALS TRUE
-- married and in the same household, but the regulations disregard the marriage (s 39(3)(a)) and we are not living together as if married
#ASSERT `Under section 39(3), are the other person and I a couple once the regulations are applied` TRUE TRUE FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: yes` `s 1(1) what I know: no` `s 39(3) the regulations say nothing about it in our case` EQUALS FALSE
-- no regulations apply: the plain test of s 39(1)
#ASSERT `Under section 39(3), are the other person and I a couple once the regulations are applied` TRUE TRUE FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: no` `s 1(1) what I know: no` `s 39(3) the regulations say nothing about it in our case` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 39(3), are the other person and I a couple once the regulations are applied` FALSE TRUE FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: no` `s 1(1) what I know: no` `s 39(3) the regulations say nothing about it in our case` EQUALS FALSE
-- s 39(3)(c): the regulations treat people who share a home as not members of the same household, so they are not a couple under (a)
#ASSERT `Under section 39(3), are the other person and I a couple once the regulations are applied` TRUE TRUE FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: no` `s 1(1) what I know: no` `s 39(3) the regulations treat us as not members of the same household` EQUALS FALSE
-- s 40: a person under 16
#ASSERT `Under section 40, is this person a child` 15 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 40, is this person a child` 16 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 40, is this person a child` 0 EQUALS TRUE

§ `Schedules 1 and 2 -- supplementary powers, and the amendments that bring in universal credit`

-- sch 1 para 4(5): includes each one's separate capital and income, subject to (6): regulations may disregard it. Arguments: joint claimants, regulations disregard mine
#ASSERT `Under schedule 1 paragraph 4(5), does our joint capital and income include my separate capital and income` TRUE `s 1(1) what I know: no` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 1 paragraph 4(5), does our joint capital and income include my separate capital and income` TRUE `s 1(1) what I know: yes` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 1 paragraph 4(5), does our joint capital and income include my separate capital and income` TRUE `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 1 paragraph 4(5), does our joint capital and income include my separate capital and income` FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: no` EQUALS NOTHING
-- sch 1 para 6(3): the voucher may not exceed the total of the amounts for the costs: equal is allowed, one more is not
#ASSERT `Under schedule 1 paragraph 6(3), is the amount paid by means of the voucher permitted` 100 100 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 1 paragraph 6(3), is the amount paid by means of the voucher permitted` 101 100 EQUALS FALSE
-- sch 1 para 7: where regulations so provide, a claimant with a right to reside who would otherwise fall within section 19, 20 or 21 is treated as not falling within it. Arguments: right to reside, would otherwise fall within, regulations so provide
#ASSERT `Under schedule 1 paragraph 7, am I treated as not falling within section 19, 20 or 21` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 1 paragraph 7, am I treated as not falling within section 19, 20 or 21` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` `s 1(1) what I know: no` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 1 paragraph 7, am I treated as not falling within section 19, 20 or 21` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under schedule 1 paragraph 7, am I treated as not falling within section 19, 20 or 21` `s 1(1) what I know: no` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under schedule 1 paragraph 7, am I treated as not falling within section 19, 20 or 21` `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` `s 1(1) what I know: yes` EQUALS NOTHING
-- sch 1 para 8(a): regulations may treat a person as having or not having a good reason. Arguments: in fact had one, regulations apply to me, they treat me as having one
-- no regulation: the plain fact
#ASSERT `Under schedule 1 paragraph 8(a), am I treated as having had a good reason` FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: I do not know` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- a regulation treats me as not having one
#ASSERT `Under schedule 1 paragraph 8(a), am I treated as having had a good reason` TRUE `s 1(1) what I know: yes` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- a regulation treats me as having one
#ASSERT `Under schedule 1 paragraph 8(a), am I treated as having had a good reason` FALSE `s 1(1) what I know: yes` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- the regulations do not apply to me: the plain fact
#ASSERT `Under schedule 1 paragraph 8(a), am I treated as having had a good reason` TRUE `s 1(1) what I know: no` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- sch 2 SSAA 159D(2): from the commencing date the amount is the amount entitled to after the alteration, without a further decision. Arguments: award in force, an alteration affects it, an exception applies, my entitlement afterwards, the commencing date, the day asked about
