§ `Sections 117 to 119: loss of benefit for a benefit offence`

-- Under section 117(2), is this benefit a disqualifying benefit?
#ASSERT `Under section 117(2), this benefit is a disqualifying benefit` `child tax credit` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 117(2), this benefit is a disqualifying benefit` `universal credit` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Conviction facts in the order the seat question asks them:
-- place, conspiracy to defraud, prescribed offence, prescribed circumstances, overpayment found, sentence, months of sentence, months the offence ran.
-- 6B(14)(a): the common law offence of conspiracy to defraud, in England and Wales, is a relevant offence.
#ASSERT `Under section 118(5), the offence is a relevant offence` `England outside Greater London` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) NOTHING `s 118(5) SSFA 6B(14)(b)(ii) some other sentence` 0 NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 6B(14)(b) is a prescribed offence committed in prescribed circumstances, AND one of (i) to (iii).
-- (i): the court found an overpayment of at least 50,000 pounds.
#ASSERT `Under section 118(5), the offence is a relevant offence` `England outside Greater London` FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST 50000) `s 118(5) SSFA 6B(14)(b)(ii) some other sentence` 0 NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (ii): a custodial sentence of at least one year (12 months).
#ASSERT `Under section 118(5), the offence is a relevant offence` `England outside Greater London` FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING `s 118(5) SSFA 6B(14)(b)(ii) a custodial sentence` 12 NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (iii): the court found the offence committed over at least two years (24 months).
#ASSERT `Under section 118(5), the offence is a relevant offence` `England outside Greater London` FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING `s 118(5) SSFA 6B(14)(b)(ii) some other sentence` 0 (JUST 24) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The same facts for an offence regulations do not prescribe: the text says no in its own words ("a prescribed offence").
#ASSERT `Under section 118(5), the offence is a relevant offence` `England outside Greater London` FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST 50000) `s 118(5) SSFA 6B(14)(b)(ii) some other sentence` 0 NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Whether regulations prescribe the offence is not known: NOTHING, never FALSE.
#ASSERT `Under section 118(5), the offence is a relevant offence` `England outside Greater London` FALSE NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST 50000) `s 118(5) SSFA 6B(14)(b)(ii) some other sentence` 0 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- Arguments as for Under section 118(5): place, conspiracy to defraud, prescribed offence, prescribed circumstances, overpayment found, sentence, months of sentence, months the offence ran.
-- A relevant offence (conspiracy to defraud in England and Wales): the section 7 restrictions do not apply.
#ASSERT `Under section 118(7), the restrictions in section 7 do not apply to me` `England outside Greater London` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) NOTHING `s 118(5) SSFA 6B(14)(b)(ii) some other sentence` 0 NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A relevant offence by 6B(14)(b)(ii): a prescribed offence in prescribed circumstances punished by a custodial sentence of at least one year.
#ASSERT `Under section 118(7), the restrictions in section 7 do not apply to me` `England outside Greater London` FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING `s 118(5) SSFA 6B(14)(b)(ii) a custodial sentence` 12 NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not a relevant offence: 7(1A) says the restrictions do not apply if it is one, and is silent otherwise, so NOTHING and never FALSE.
#ASSERT `Under section 118(7), the restrictions in section 7 do not apply to me` `England outside Greater London` FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST 50000) `s 118(5) SSFA 6B(14)(b)(ii) some other sentence` 0 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- Whether the offence is a relevant offence is not known: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `Under section 118(7), the restrictions in section 7 do not apply to me` `England outside Greater London` FALSE NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST 50000) `s 118(5) SSFA 6B(14)(b)(ii) some other sentence` 0 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

