#ASSERT `Under section 127(4), information about me held for departmental functions can be supplied` TRUE `s 127(1)(a) the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs` `s 127(4) the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs or a person providing services to them` `s 127(4) the purposes of HMRC functions` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 127(4), information about me held for departmental functions can be supplied` TRUE `s 127(3)(a) the Secretary of State or a person providing services to the Secretary of State` `s 127(4) the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs or a person providing services to them` `s 127 some other purpose` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 127(4), information about me held for departmental functions can be supplied` FALSE `s 127(3)(a) the Secretary of State or a person providing services to the Secretary of State` `s 127(4) the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs or a person providing services to them` `s 127(4) the purposes of HMRC functions` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 128(1), can the Secretary of State supply information about me?
#ASSERT `Under section 128(1), the Secretary of State can supply information about me` `s 128(1) the Secretary of State` `s 128(1) social security information` `s 128(2)(a) the Director of Public Prosecutions` `s 128(3)(b) the giving of advice on any matter relating to criminal proceedings, or criminal offences, which relate wholly or partly to social security matters or child support` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 128(1), the Secretary of State can supply information about me` `s 128 some other supplier` `s 128(1) social security information` `s 128(2)(a) the Director of Public Prosecutions` `s 128(3)(b) the giving of advice on any matter relating to criminal proceedings, or criminal offences, which relate wholly or partly to social security matters or child support` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Arguments in the order the seat asks: supplied under section 128, discloser is that person or their employee, relates to a particular person,
-- kind of disclosure, contravenes the Director's restriction, information about section 2 ETA 1973 schemes, another Act provides otherwise.
-- The bar applies on its own words and nothing in (2), (3) or (4) displaces it.
#ASSERT `Under section 129(1), the bar on disclosure applies to the disclosure of my information` TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 129(2) a disclosure of some other kind` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 129(2)(i): a disclosure made with the consent of each person to whom the information relates is outside the bar.
#ASSERT `Under section 129(1), the bar on disclosure applies to the disclosure of my information` TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 129(2)(i) a disclosure made with the consent of each person to whom the information relates` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 129(3): information about ETA 1973 section 2 schemes is outside the bar.
#ASSERT `Under section 129(1), the bar on disclosure applies to the disclosure of my information` TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 129(2) a disclosure of some other kind` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 129(2)(b): a disclosure for a function of the Director is outside the bar only where it contravenes no restriction of the Director.
#ASSERT `Under section 129(1), the bar on disclosure applies to the disclosure of my information` TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 129(2)(b) a disclosure made for the purposes of a function of the Director of Public Prosecutions` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 129(1), the bar on disclosure applies to the disclosure of my information` TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 129(2)(b) a disclosure made for the purposes of a function of the Director of Public Prosecutions` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 129(4): another Act may provide otherwise, and what it provides is outside the text: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `Under section 129(1), the bar on disclosure applies to the disclosure of my information` TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 129(2) a disclosure of some other kind` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The bar is on a person to whom information is supplied under section 128: for any other holder the text is silent, so NOTHING and never FALSE.
#ASSERT `Under section 129(1), the bar on disclosure applies to the disclosure of my information` FALSE TRUE TRUE `s 129(2) a disclosure of some other kind` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Arguments as for Under section 129(1), then: did the person make the disclosure.
-- The bar applies and the person made the disclosure: an offence.
#ASSERT `Under section 129(5), the person who disclosed my information commits an offence` TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 129(2) a disclosure of some other kind` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The bar applies but the person made no disclosure: NOTHING (the subsection speaks of "a person who contravenes subsection (1)").
#ASSERT `Under section 129(5), the person who disclosed my information commits an offence` TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 129(2) a disclosure of some other kind` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The disclosure was made with the consent of everyone it relates to (129(2)(i)), so the bar does not apply: NOTHING, not FALSE.
#ASSERT `Under section 129(5), the person who disclosed my information commits an offence` TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 129(2)(i) a disclosure made with the consent of each person to whom the information relates` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Another Act may provide otherwise (129(4)) and what it provides is outside the text: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `Under section 129(5), the person who disclosed my information commits an offence` TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 129(2) a disclosure of some other kind` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING


§ `Sections 130 to 132: information held by local authorities`

-- Arguments: a local authority holds it, what the information is, prescribed, receiving a relevant service, what the authority does, purposes about a relevant benefit, who is given it.
-- The authority uses it itself for the payment of a relevant benefit to the individual.
#ASSERT `Under section 130(5), the local authority can use or supply information about me` TRUE `s 130(2)(a) information as to the fact of the provision or likely provision of the service` NOTHING TRUE `s 130(5)(a) itself uses the information` TRUE `s 130(6)(c) a local authority` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- It supplies it to a person listed in 130(6).
#ASSERT `Under section 130(5), the local authority can use or supply information about me` TRUE `s 130(2)(a) information as to the fact of the provision or likely provision of the service` NOTHING TRUE `s 130(5)(b) supplies the information to another person` TRUE `s 130(6)(a) the Secretary of State` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- It supplies it to someone not listed: NOTHING (the subsection says nothing of other supply).
#ASSERT `Under section 130(5), the local authority can use or supply information about me` TRUE `s 130(2)(a) information as to the fact of the provision or likely provision of the service` NOTHING TRUE `s 130(5)(b) supplies the information to another person` TRUE `s 130(6) some other person` EQUALS NOTHING
-- No local authority holds it, or the information is not of the kind in 130(2): section 130 does not apply, so NOTHING.
#ASSERT `Under section 130(5), the local authority can use or supply information about me` FALSE `s 130(2)(a) information as to the fact of the provision or likely provision of the service` NOTHING TRUE `s 130(5)(a) itself uses the information` TRUE `s 130(6)(c) a local authority` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 130(5), the local authority can use or supply information about me` TRUE `s 130(2) some other information` (JUST TRUE) TRUE `s 130(5)(a) itself uses the information` TRUE `s 130(6)(c) a local authority` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Arguments: the supplier is the Secretary of State or a provider to them, the information is relevant information, which description fits the recipient, whether the Secretary of State prescribes the recipient, whether the purpose is prescribed.
#ASSERT `Under section 131(1), the Secretary of State can supply information about me to a qualifying person` TRUE TRUE `s 131(11)(a) a local authority` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 131(1), the Secretary of State can supply information about me to a qualifying person` TRUE TRUE `s 131(11)(g) a person prescribed or of a description prescribed by the Secretary of State` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Whether a prescribed person is a qualifying person is not known: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `Under section 131(1), the Secretary of State can supply information about me to a qualifying person` TRUE TRUE `s 131(11)(g) a person prescribed or of a description prescribed by the Secretary of State` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not a qualifying person: 131(1) speaks only of a qualifying person, so NOTHING.
#ASSERT `Under section 131(1), the Secretary of State can supply information about me to a qualifying person` TRUE TRUE `s 131(11) some other person` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 131(1), the Secretary of State can supply information about me to a qualifying person` FALSE TRUE `s 131(11)(a) a local authority` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Arguments: which description of person fits the discloser, without lawful authority, the information came by virtue of 131(1), (3) or (4), the information relates to a particular person.
#ASSERT `Under section 132(1), the person who disclosed my information is guilty of an offence` `s 132(2)(a) a person mentioned in section 131(11)(a) to (c)` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 132(1), the person who disclosed my information is guilty of an offence` `s 132(2)(d) a person who is or has been an employee of a person mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b)` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not a person described in 132(2), or one of the other conditions is not met: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `Under section 132(1), the person who disclosed my information is guilty of an offence` `s 132(2) some other person` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 132(1), the person who disclosed my information is guilty of an offence` `s 132(2)(a) a person mentioned in section 131(11)(a) to (c)` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 132(1), the person who disclosed my information is guilty of an offence` `s 132(2)(a) a person mentioned in section 131(11)(a) to (c)` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
